From a3f249ebc101fc4525776dfde2e5d6c3dc8b8014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <winshyon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:43:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(provider): allow overriding the system provider directory

DiscoverProviders() always scanned the hard-coded system directory
/usr/libexec/complytime/providers after the user directory, so unit
tests that expect an empty or controlled provider set failed on hosts
with providers installed from RPM packages.

Add the COMPLYTIME_SYSTEM_PROVIDER_DIR environment variable, resolved
by complytime.ResolveSystemProviderDir(), following the existing env
override pattern (XDG_DATA_HOME, COMPLYTIME_WORKSPACE). Discovery and
the doctor "no providers found" message use the resolved path.

Tests that assume no system providers now point the variable at an
empty temporary directory, and a new test covers discovery from an
overridden system directory including user-directory precedence.

Fixes #881

Assisted-by: Claude Code
